#: src/postulo/templates/help/documents.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>CVs and portfolios</em> are variants of your career record: each one chooses which entries to show, in which order, and how they are set. Correct an entry in <em>Your career</em> and every variant changes with it. <em>Letters</em> are the cover and motivation letters, with their own text."
msgstr "<em>CV e portfolios</em> èn variantas da Voss percurs professiunal: mintgina tscherna tge inscripziuns mussar, en tge urden e co ch'ellas èn cumponidas. Curregiai ina inscripziun en <em>Voss percurs</em> e mintga varianta sa mida cun ella. <em>Brevs</em> èn las brevs d'accumpagnament e da motivaziun, cun lur agen text."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/documents.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Files</em> are documents you kept as they came: a diploma, a certificate, a reference letter. They can be marked as the proof of an entry of your career, and sent with an application. <em>Sent documents</em> are copies of what went out, exactly as it went, kept unchanged so that you can see later what you claimed."
msgstr "<em>Datotecas</em> èn documents che Vus avais conservà sco ch'els èn arrivads: in diplom, in certificat, ina brev da recumandaziun. Ellas pon vegnir marcadas sco cumprova d'ina inscripziun da Voss percurs e tramessas cun ina candidatura. <em>Documents tramess</em> èn copias da quai ch'è partì, exactamain sco ch'el è partì, conservadas senza midadas, uschia che Vus pudais vesair pli tard tge che Vus avais pretendì."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/contact_block.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Headline</em> is a short professional title, such as “Backend engineer”. A CV that has a headline of its own prints that one instead."
msgstr "<em>Titel professiunal</em> è in curt titel professiunal, sco p.ex. «Inschignier backend». In CV che ha ses agen titel professiunal mussa quel enstagl."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/career.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Import</em> reads a Europass CV; <em>Export</em> writes your details and your career as one file you can keep or move to another Postulo; <em>Preview</em> shows the whole record as a document, and <em>Your CVs</em> opens the variants made from it."
msgstr "<em>Importar</em> legia in CV Europass; <em>Exportar</em> scriva Vossas datas e Voss percurs en ina datoteca che Vus pudais conservar u transferir en in auter Postulo; <em>Prevista</em> mussa l'entir dossier sco document, e <em>Voss CV</em> avra las variantas fatgas a basa da quel."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/identifiers.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Kind</em> is the register the identifier belongs to, and <em>What goes where</em> shows what each one looks like. <em>Other</em> takes anything else, with a name you give it."
msgstr "<em>Tip</em> è il register al qual l'identificatur appartegna, e <em>Tge va nua</em> mussa co che mintgin para ora. <em>Auter</em> accepta tut il rest, cun in num che Vus al dais."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/telephone_numbers.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Kind</em> says what the number is, and can be left blank. Choose <em>Other</em> and a box asks what to call it."
msgstr "<em>Tip</em> inditga tge numer ch'i è e po vegnir laschà vid. Tschernai <em>Auter</em> ed in champ dumonda co al numnar."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/contact_block.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Language of your career record</em> says which language your experience, education and projects are typed in. A CV in another language shows what you have translated and says what it could not. It also decides which forms of address and pronouns the menus of <em>Your name</em> offer. Left as it is, it follows the language you read Postulo in."
msgstr "<em>Lingua da Voss percurs professiunal</em> inditga en tge lingua che Vossas experientschas, Vossa furmaziun e Voss projects èn endatads. In CV en in'autra lingua mussa quai che Vus avais translatà e di tge ch'el n'ha betg pudì. Ella decida er tge furmas d'allocuziun e tge pronoms ch'ils menus da <em>Voss num</em> porschan. Sche Vus la laschais sco ch'ella è, suonda ella la lingua en la quala Vus legiais Postulo."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/contact_block.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Location</em> is where you are, as a document should print it. Left blank, your documents print the town and country of your primary postal address, never the street, and the box shows that line in grey. The blank is what is kept, so making another address the primary changes what is printed without this page being saved again. Type something and that is printed instead."
msgstr "<em>Lieu</em> è nua che Vus essas, sco ch'in document duai al mussar. Sch'el è vid, mussan Voss documents il lieu ed il pajais da Vossa adressa postala principala, mai la via, ed il champ mussa quella lingia en grisch. Quai che vegn conservà è il champ vid, uschia che sche Vus fixais in'autra adressa sco principala, sa mida quai ch'è stampà senza che questa pagina stoppia vegnir arcunada danovamain. Endatai insatge, e quai vegn stampà enstagl."

#: src/postulo/templates/help/links.html
#, fuzzy
msgid "<em>Other</em> takes any web address, and a name to show for it; left blank, the name is the address's host. A card with no <em>Service</em> menu takes any address in the same way. Under a named service a row has no name of its own: the service is its name."
msgstr "<em>Auter</em> accepta mintga adressa d'internet ed in num per la mussar; sch'el è vid, è il num il host da l'adressa. Ina carta senza menu <em>Servetsch</em> accepta mintga adressa a la medema moda. Sut in servetsch numnà n'ha ina lingia nagin agen num: il servetsch è ses num."

